* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.pdf binary
# 6 Nov 2026. The archive CSVs are append-mostly and written on two machines (the
# laptop and GitHub Actions). With git's default merge, a conflicting hunk from the
# other side was thrown away by `pull --rebase -X theirs` / `-X ours`, which deleted
# 7,215 committed rows between 24 Oct and 6 Nov. The built-in union driver keeps the
# lines of both sides; archive.load_all and archive.export drop duplicate keys.
data/archive/**/*.csv merge=union
